WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.967
Former New Jersey Governor

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:01.568
Chris Christie

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.003
launched his primary campaign

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.771
tonight in Manchester, New Hampshire,

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:05.705
and aimed at straight

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.340
the former president

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:11.478
a lonely, self consumed

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:16.116
self-serving

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.451
mirror hog

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:22.122
is not a leader.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:24.657
Well, let me be clear, in case

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:27.093
I have not been already

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:31.264
the person I am talking about

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:33.800
who is obsessed with the mirror,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.236
who never admits a mistake,

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:38.738
who never admits a fault,

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:40.540
and who always find someone else

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.875
and something else

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:43.977
to blame for whatever goes wrong,

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:46.446
but finds every reason to take credit

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.948
for anything that goes right.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.418
Is Donald Trump

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.455
and if we don't have

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:58.158
that conversation with you,

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:02.529
we don't deserve to ask for your vote.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.731
We don't deserve

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:06.933
the mantle of leadership.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.202
We don't deserve

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:12.005
to have you think of us

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:13.807
as people worthy of leadership.

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:15.542
As former

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.776
Governor Christie tonight,

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.578
he has famously had a bumpy history

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.446
with the former president

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:20.346
who was sharply critical

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:21.214
during the 2016

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:22.582
primaries and dropped out,

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:24.451
reentered the fold as a born again

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:25.251
Trump supporter,

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.286
then broke with him again

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:27.720
after January six.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:28.621
Here's a sampling

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:29.756
of some of the tough words

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.324
he's had for the former president

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.559
in the 2016 race

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:35.095
and the run up to tonight

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:36.930
he gets criticized

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:37.964
he can't take it

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:40.266
he is jamming to Trump Tower and phones.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.702
I'm happy to take any observations he has

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.070
even if he can only do them

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.705
in 140 characters or less.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:48.441
When you say that it is patriotic

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.211
to suspend the constitution

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.312
if you believe the election

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:53.513
is being stolen from you

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:54.914
that person is disqualified

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.649
in my view from the United States.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:02:00.053
Can we keep losing and losing and losing.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:02.355
And the

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:02.789
fact of

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:06.259
the matter is the reason we're losing

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:08.528
is because Donald Trump

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:12.265
has put himself before everybody else.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:13.900
The question now

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.068
and it's no longer academic,

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.369
how will he turn that critique

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:17.337
into primary votes?

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.204
Joining us tonight, CNN

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.172
political commentator, former

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.373
Obama special adviser Van

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.808
Jones, former Georgia Republican

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.476
Lieutenant Governor Jeff Duncan.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.411
Also CNN chief political analyst

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.179
Gloria Borger.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:26.479
Gloria,

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:27.013
what does Governor

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:28.081
Christie believe his lane

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.415
in this race is?

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.184
Well, we always ask about these lanes.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.086
And I was talking to a senior adviser

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:33.553
to Christie

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:35.021
and asked him that exact question

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.189
and he said

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:39.092
Chris Lane is going through Trump.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:42.095
It is the only way someone can win.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.397
And as you saw today,

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:45.832
what Chris Christie did was

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:46.966
take him on frontally,

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:48.368
which quite frankly,

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.670
the other candidates are not yet doing

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:52.906
in a way that Chris Christie is doing it.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:53.740
Remember, how

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:57.610
he took on Marco Rubio in 2016

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.112
and that infamous debate

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:00.914
and kind of destroyed him.

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.582
He may have destroyed Marco Rubio

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.750
but he also destroyed

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.451
himself in the process.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:06.186
And I think that's

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:08.221
a little bit of the danger here

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:10.089
because he's not really popular

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:11.391
with the Republican

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:12.892
electorate at this point.

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:15.028
So he has to ingratiate himself

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.196
to Republicans

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:18.631
while taking on their favorite soldier,

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:21.201
Lieutenant Governor Duncan.

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.802
Do you think he has a lead?

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:23.636
Yeah, I certainly do.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:24.804
I mean, what I heard tonight

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.339
was somebody who wants to win

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:27.707
but not afraid to lose.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.042
I think that's a dangerous combination

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:29.676
for somebody

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:31.211
like Donald Trump to have to face that

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:32.345
that type of music.

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:33.046
I think Chris Christie

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:35.048
needs to stick to the stick to the script

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:37.083
that he was a two time governor

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.618
in a blue state.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:39.719
He's been a Republican longer

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.020
than Donald Trump ever has.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.655
I think he needs to stick to that script

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:43.556
and continue to hammer.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:44.557
It's interesting then because, I mean,

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.725
Chris Christie has pushed

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:46.593
against this notion

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.894
that he's simply,

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:48.595
you know,

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:49.162
going to attack

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:50.396
Donald Trump in the primary.

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:51.931
He says he wouldn't run

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:52.632
if he didn't believe

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:55.034
he could actually win this thing.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:55.868
He's got the same chance

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:56.903
of getting the Republican nomination

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:57.737
as he has gotten

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:58.671
the Democratic nomination.

00:03:58.671 --> 00:03:58.805
I mean,

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:01.541
he has no support in that party

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:02.842
that even rival

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:03.476
some of the people

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:04.444
who are in the single digits.

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:06.512
So I think it's important for the country

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.580
that he's doing it.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.016
I think it's important for the country

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:12.785
that somebody with his backbone

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.821
and courage does challenge the president.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.556
It's been remarkable to me

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:17.290
to see someone

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.091
like Donald Trump

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.525
who lost the White House,

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:20.893
lost in midterms,

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:22.428
basically be able to skate by even people

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:22.895
who want to be

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:23.730
president are scared to say

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:24.530
anything bad about him.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.099
So I think it's good for the country.

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:26.599
But the chances

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:27.300
that his chance

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.868
of getting the nomination, this party,

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:29.902
he has about the same chance

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:30.436
to get nomination.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:31.571
This party's he does a Green Party.

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:33.373
Any other party. No, zero.

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:34.974
Gloria, Christie's relationship

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:35.842
with the former president's

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:37.277
obviously been a roller coaster.

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:38.311
Does that

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:39.846
give him a credibility problem

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:40.847
with voters?

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:43.049
Yeah, I think I think it obviously does.

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:43.283
I mean,

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:45.084
we all remember that he was prepping

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:45.752
Donald Trump

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:46.486
for the debate

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:49.055
when he famously caught COVID

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:50.456
after that debate.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.592
And he was supporting Donald Trump.

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.060
And then he turned on him

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.261
after January six

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.297
and his advisers said to me, look,

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:59.198
we're going to make that distinction

00:04:59.198 --> 00:04:59.866
that after

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:01.200
January six, Chris

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.702
Christie could no longer

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.437
support Donald Trump.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:05.638
But there is a flip side

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:06.539
to this, Anderson,

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:08.574
which is he's out there already saying,

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:10.410
I know Donald Trump

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.611
better than most of you,

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:14.113
so I can testify firsthand

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.416
about what kind of human being he is

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:18.818
and what kind of president he would be

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:20.853
if he's elected. This next time.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:22.989
So it kind of works both ways,

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:25.124
but he does have to get over that hump of

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:26.693
why were you so close to him

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:27.894
and now you hate him.

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:29.228
Do you think, Governor,

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.563
do you think the race

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:31.264
that there are too many

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:33.032
candidates already?

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.767
Well, look, I'm one of those Republicans.

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:35.768
I said this earlier today.

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:36.903
I'm excited to see qualified

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:37.837
candidates show up.

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:38.438
And I think we've got

00:05:38.438 --> 00:05:39.872
to put our best foot forward.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:40.173
You know,

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:41.774
I'm just also one of those Republicans

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:42.775
who think the weight of gravity

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:44.077
is going to catch up to Donald Trump.

00:05:44.077 --> 00:05:44.944
I mean, he's going to have three

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:46.245
or four indictments

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.580
that are going to be wrapped around him

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.048
all the way through this entire process.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:49.916
And I think we've got to have

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:51.617
somebody who's qualified and ready to go.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:51.751
Right.

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:53.019
But even with three or four indictments,

00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:54.787
if you got a whole bunch of candidates

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:56.222
who divide up vote,

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:56.956
you know,

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.091
those who don't want Trump

00:05:58.091 --> 00:06:00.393
and Trump has a base of 30 35%

00:06:00.927 --> 00:06:02.028
is not inevitable.

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:03.062
It's a math problem.

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:03.930
But you're never going to limit

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:04.397
this field

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:05.064
out of the gates

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:06.833
for three or four candidates.

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:07.367
So you're going to have

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:08.101
a whole slew of them.

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:09.302
You're going to have to have cream rise

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:10.169
at the top.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:11.371
I think a guy like Chris Christie,

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:11.971
I think

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:13.473
Tim Scott, Nikki Haley,

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:14.474
Ron DeSantis,

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:15.541
these are qualified candidates

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.610
that could legitimately win a nomination.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:18.411
But you've got to have Donald

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:19.212
Trump fall apart

00:06:19.212 --> 00:06:20.613
and I think that's possible.

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:21.280
The problem is,

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:21.881
I mean, cream rise

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:22.782
to the top of the froth

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:24.517
stays around for a long time.

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:25.017
You know,

00:06:25.118 --> 00:06:26.853
like some people can run with no money

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:28.054
and just keep showing up

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:28.688
and saying, well,

00:06:28.688 --> 00:06:29.856
I mean, if you look at

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:31.891
what happened to the Democratic Party,

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:33.993
Bernie Sanders was getting out front

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:36.662
scared shit out of everybody.

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:38.598
As soon as one person

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:39.932
got ahead with Biden,

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:41.401
everybody just dropped out.

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:42.869
And so there is at least

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:45.271
an example in the

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:47.407
modern context of a party

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:48.441
coming to its senses.

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:48.674
You know,

00:06:48.674 --> 00:06:50.643
I love Bernie Sanders, who doesn't?

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:51.544
But people in the party

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:52.044
didn't feel like

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:53.846
he should be the standard bearer.

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:55.214
Biden won,

00:06:55.214 --> 00:06:57.049
and then Cory Booker dropped out.

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:57.850
Everybody else dropped out.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.719
Somebody got to beat

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:02.021
Donald Trump in one of these races.

00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:04.290
And whoever that person is

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.025
could make a credible case.

00:07:06.025 --> 00:07:07.660
The rest of you guys get out of my way.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.061
Let me go one on one.

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:10.329
But nobody's going to drop out

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:11.197
before somebody

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:11.697
who's actually put

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:12.932
a win on the scoreboard.

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:14.100
Gloria, I mean, the first Republican

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.468
primary debate is in August.

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:16.602
Do you think Christie has enough time

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:18.404
to qualify between then and now?

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:19.172
And also,

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:20.606
would he commit

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:21.674
to the RNC rule

00:07:21.674 --> 00:07:22.642
supporting the eventual

00:07:22.642 --> 00:07:23.543
Republican nominee?

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:25.411
I think that's a good question.

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:27.313
It's unanswered right now.

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:29.549
They refuse to answer that.

00:07:29.549 --> 00:07:30.616
I think Chris Christie,

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:31.818
it's a high bar for him.

00:07:31.818 --> 00:07:33.686
He's not popular right now

00:07:33.686 --> 00:07:34.854
in the Republican Party,

00:07:34.854 --> 00:07:36.889
but he has to get on that debate stage.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:39.759
He has to be able to take on Donald Trump

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:41.494
if Donald Trump participates.

00:07:41.494 --> 00:07:42.862
Remember, Donald Trump is saying,

00:07:42.862 --> 00:07:43.463
you know,

00:07:43.463 --> 00:07:44.497
why would I show up

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:45.264
if I've got such

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:46.999
a large percentage of the vote

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:48.401
he needs to go mano

00:07:48.401 --> 00:07:49.769
a mano with Donald Trump

00:07:49.769 --> 00:07:50.670
and I

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:51.437
right now

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:53.539
can't see how he's going to get

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:54.273
to do that.

00:07:54.273 --> 00:07:55.541
I don't think Trump wants

00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:57.710
to share a debate stage with him.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.912
That would be pretty toxic to watch.

00:07:59.912 --> 00:08:00.880
All right. Appreciate it all.

